      "strings": {
        "brief": "You're on an authorised exercise at Merrin & Sallow Architects, a fictional practice. A feed and an inbox are waiting: some posts are fine, some give too much away, and some messages were made to pull work details out of you. Sort them, close the gaps, and report the fakes. Reporting or checking when you're unsure is always fine and never marked down.",
        "flipMissedHeading": "Nothing to replay this time",
        "flipLandedNoTells": "It read as an ordinary note from a colleague, with nothing in it to question. Next, you spot the same moves in a feed and an inbox, and close the gaps.",
        "noBlameLine": "A convincing profile of a person is built from scraps anyone could find. Nobody is foolish for having posted them; the fix is a setting and a pause, not shame.",
        "defendIntro": "Go through the inbox and decide what to do with each message, mark the feed drafts Post, Tweak or Hold, and tighten your own settings. A friendly opener that steers to your firm's systems or who runs IT is still reconnaissance; report it. There's no clock on you here.",
        "mondayCard": "On Monday: tighten one privacy setting today, and check what's behind you before your next post or video call. And if a stranger asks about your firm's systems or who runs IT, share nothing and report it using the route in the box below.",
        "defendOnly": "A well-made message is built from scraps anyone could find online, and anyone can be pulled in by one. The ones you were caught out by are shown below, with what gave each one away."
      },
      "debrief": {
        "mondayCard": "slot:customer_report_route",
        "noBlameLine": true
      },
      "sortDrill": {
